    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1840A\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to information cable\ntelevision companies must provide to subscribers regarding availability\nof required equipment at retail\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo notify cable customers of their options regarding certain equipment\nrequired for cable subscriptions, including how such equipment , includ-\ning modems, can be purchased at retail.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 4 of section 224-a to add a new paragraph\n(d) that requires cable television companies to provide notice regarding\nequipment, including modems, required for subscriptions.\n\nSection 2: Effective Date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCable providers charge customers for services that are dependent on the\nuse of leased equipment from the same service provider, such as a modem,\nremote control and other device. While some consumers have the option of\npurchasing their own modems, many may not be aware of other options and\nsome choose to lease as part of a service package.\n\nThis bill would require cable companies to provide information to\nsubscribers that details how or where such equipment can be purchased\noutright and what retail equipment would be compatible with the cable\nsystem.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSenate\n\n2020: S4519A - Referred to Energy and Telecommunications\n\nAssembly\n\n2020: A1416C - Ordered to Third Reading cal.73\n\n2017-18: A3025 - referred to corporations, authorities and commissions\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
